<div class="row mb-5 align-items-center g-4">
    <div class="col-lg-5 order-lg-1">
        <div class="vitrum-container module-feature-img border-0">
            <img src="~/images/vitrum/glass-magnifying-glass.webp" alt="Pharmacist verifying a prescription" class="vitrum-img" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-7 order-lg-2">
        <p class="section-kicker">Counter first</p>
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-3">Built for the dispensary floor</h2>
        <p>
            Quick Dispense is designed for keyboard-speed work: till and currency, patient search,
            doctor/referrer (including MDPCZ register), multi-line medicines with dosage cyphers,
            optional refills, script photo or PDF capture, then Save → Verify → Collect/Pay.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-0">
            Status is workflow — Dispensed, Verified, Collected, Awaiting POS, On Hold — while the
            script number stays permanent from the first save. Labels and dispense PDFs print at the
            till; unpaid shortfalls surface on POS without a second system.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5 align-items-center g-4">
    <div class="col-lg-7">
        <p class="section-kicker">Clinical continuum</p>
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-3">EHR that feeds the pharmacy shelf</h2>
        <p>
            Clinic prescriptions share the same patient and product master as retail dispensing.
            Encounters, appointments, labs, admissions, and surgery bookings can link straight into
            billing. Drug-interaction rules, allergy flags, and ICD-10/CPT coding keep documentation
            audit-ready for regulated practice.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-0">
            Whether you run a standalone pharmacy, a day clinic, or a full hospital, BasaRx scales
            the same data model — so growth does not mean a migration to another vendor.
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-5">
        <div class="vitrum-container module-feature-img border-0">
            <img src="~/images/vitrum/glass-shield.webp" alt="Electronic health records and clinical safety" class="vitrum-img" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

